From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vijay Pothukuchi <vijayp@ti.com>
Date: Wed, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: ti: k3-j784s4: Keep display chain enabled in
 vision-apps overlay

The k3-j784s4-vision-apps overlay unconditionally disables the display
chain (dss, mhdp/DP bridge, serdes_wiz4, main_i2c4) to prevent the A72
Linux driver from conflicting with automotive R5 ownership in
PSDK Analytics configurations.

With PSDK Analytics 11.02.x SYSFW using TI_SCI_PD_SHARED for the display
power domains (see preceding patch), the A72 host can co-own these power
domains alongside the automotive R5 host.  Remove the four display-chain
disable fragments from the overlay so that TIDSS, MHDP/DP, SerDes and
the main_i2c4 GPIO expander (which drives DP0 power and HPD) are all
accessible from Linux.

Nodes removed from the overlay disable list:
  - dss@4a00000    (TIDSS display controller)
  - bridge@a000000 (MHDP/DP output bridge, alias "mhdp")
  - serdes_wiz4    (SerDes WIZ wrapper for DP physical layer)
  - i2c@2040000   (main_i2c4, carries exp4 TCA6408 for DP0 power/HPD)

Nodes deliberately kept disabled (automotive R5 domain only):
  - main_i2c1, main_i2c5 (not needed for DP0 display)
  - ti_csi2rx0/1/2 (camera interfaces, owned by automotive R5)

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TI J784S4 EVM Armbian/Linux display enablement]

Signed-off-by: Vijay Pothukuchi <vijayp@ti.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j784s4-vision-apps.dtso | 16 ----------------
 1 file changed, 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j784s4-vision-apps.dtso b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j784s4-vision-apps.dtso
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j784s4-vision-apps.dtso
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j784s4-vision-apps.dtso
@@ -14,26 +14,10 @@
     status = "disabled";
 };

-&main_i2c4 {
-	status = "disabled";
-};
-
 &main_i2c5 {
 	status = "disabled";
 };

-&dss {
-    status = "disabled";
-};
-
-&mhdp {
-    status = "disabled";
-};
-
-&serdes_wiz4 {
-    status = "disabled";
-};
-
 &ti_csi2rx0 {
     status = "disabled";
 };
